     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "5"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "caption",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The screen's five places"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The menu bar. A press opens one."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The ribbon. The commands used most are listed. The font colour, the highlight colour, the paragraph style and the alignment each open a choice on a press (press again or Esc to shut it). A group that does not fit goes into the … at the right end."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The editing area. Press here and type."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Navigation. It splits into the 3 tabs Headings, Slides and Placed."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The status bar. Where you are, what a press did, how many pages there are."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The basics of typing"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press over a character and the cursor (an upright bar) stands there. You can type from there."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Typing, and parting a line"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press where you want to type."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Type. A character no key carries goes in as it stands (an underline comes out while it is being composed)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press Enter and the paragraph parts in two there."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "At the head of the paragraph that parted, "
    },
    {
     "text": "Backspace",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " joins it onto the one in front and it is back as it was."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "slide",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "screen-area",
     "frame": {
      "x": 10.0,
      "y": 30.0,
      "w": 180.0,
      "h": 60.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "abc|de"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "screen-area",
     "frame": {
      "x": 230.0,
      "y": 30.0,
      "w": 180.0,
      "h": 60.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "Press Enter"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "screen-area",
     "frame": {
      "x": 450.0,
      "y": 20.0,
      "w": 180.0,
      "h": 40.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "abc"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "screen-area",
     "frame": {
      "x": 450.0,
      "y": 62.0,
      "w": 180.0,
      "h": 40.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "|de"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "arrow",
     "frame": {
      "x": 194.0,
      "y": 46.0,
      "w": 32.0,
      "h": 28.0
     }
    },
    {
     "style": "arrow",
     "frame": {
      "x": 414.0,
      "y": 46.0,
      "w": 32.0,
      "h": 28.0
     }
    },
    {
     "style": "number-dot",
     "frame": {
      "x": 10.0,
      "y": 100.0,
      "w": 24.0,
      "h": 24.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "number-dot",
     "frame": {
      "x": 230.0,
      "y": 100.0,
      "w": 24.0,
      "h": 24.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "number-dot",
     "frame": {
      "x": 450.0,
      "y": 108.0,
      "w": 24.0,
      "h": 24.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "3"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "caption",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Enter parts a paragraph in two (| is the cursor)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Inside a table's cell Enter does not part it. What grows the cells is “Insert a row” and “Insert a column”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Deleting"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Backspace",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " deletes the one character in front, and at a paragraph's head joins it onto the paragraph in front. "
    },
    {
     "text": "Delete",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " deletes the one character after, and at a paragraph's end joins the next paragraph on."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Selecting"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There are two ways to select."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Drag. Hold it down and move."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Hold Shift down and move an arrow key."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Type while something is selected and what is selected is "
    },
    {
     "text": "replaced",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " by what you typed. Select across paragraphs and delete, and the paragraphs crossed join into one."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+A",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " selects everything. Copying is "
    },
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+C",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ", cutting is "
    },
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+X",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ", pasting is "
    },
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+V",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ". Text brought in from outside can be pasted too."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Undoing, redoing, and doing a command again"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+Z",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " undoes one step. To redo it, "
    },
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+Shift+Z",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " or "
    },
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+Y",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "F4",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " is another thing: it does the last command again, "
    },
    {
     "text": "where the cursor is now"
    },
    {
     "text": ". Put a column in, move to another table and press "
    },
    {
     "text": "F4",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ", and a column goes into that one. Where nothing can be done again, the status bar says which command it was holding."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Doing a command again is not the same as a redo. A redo puts back a step you undid; doing it again runs the command afresh, wherever you now stand."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Text typed in one run is undone together in one step, not character by character."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "On a Mac, Command will do in place of Ctrl."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Finding and replacing"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+F",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " moves to the find field at the menu bar's right. Type and "
    },
    {
     "text": "the count found comes out on the spot",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Type the text to find. “3 found” and the like comes out to the right."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Enter moves to the next, Shift+Enter to the one before. Reach the end and it comes back to the head."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Open “Replace”, type the text to replace with, and press “Replace” or “Replace all”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Replace all is undone in one step, not one place at a time."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The count is “how many were found”. A cell holding a formula can be found but not replaced, so the count replaced can be fewer than this. The “Replaced N places” that comes out after the press is that count."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where they overlap is not counted. Find “aa” in “aaa” and it is one (the replacing side goes on from the end of what it found too, so the count and the outcome agree)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The styles of text and paragraphs"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What kspage's decorating lays on is "
    },
    {
     "text": "a style's name",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". Rather than giving a colour or a weight directly, you lay a name on."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Lay a name on and changing that name's contents in one place afterwards changes every place it was laid on."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Laying bold and italic on at once"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Bold is "
    },
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+B",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ", italic is "
    },
    {
     "text": "Ctrl+I",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ". These two go on by key alone."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "From the menu's “Style” → “Font” you can choose the colour, the highlight, "
    },
    {
     "text": "underline",
     "style": "underline"
    },
    {
     "text": ", "
    },
    {
     "text": "strikethrough",
     "style": "strikethrough"
    },
    {
     "text": ", bold and italic. Point at a row and the choice opens to the right, with a mark on what is laid on."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Every one of them carries an “Unset” row. Choose it and that one thing alone is inherited from the parent's style. To take everything laid on off, it is “Character style”'s “Unset”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A decoration that is a line does not change the measures. Laying it on does not move where the lines break."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Choosing a paragraph's style"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The style of the paragraph the cursor is in is swapped under “Paragraph style” in the menu's “Style”. In this manual that lists "
    },
    {
     "text": "body",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " · "
    },
    {
     "text": "bullet",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " · "
    },
    {
     "text": "code",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " · "
    },
    {
     "text": "warning",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " and the like."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The styles in detail, and making one"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Under “The styles in detail” in the menu's “Style” you can choose one name and reach into its contents. What can be reached is this."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Set"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "What it sets"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Font"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Font name, size, weight, italic, text colour, highlight colour, underline, strikethrough"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Paragraph"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The space before and after, the indent, the inner space, the alignment, the leading, whether it wraps"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Line and fill"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The line's thickness and colour, the fill, the shape (rounded, ellipse, triangle and 11 in all)"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Bullets and numbering"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A mark, a number, a running number, a chapter number"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "How a number is shown"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The digit grouping, the decimal places, per cent, the text put on before and after, a date's shape"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The arranging"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Flowed in, grid, absolute coordinates, the count of columns and the gap between them"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The way of gathering"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The table of contents, the footnote list, a bar chart, a line chart"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "When the value"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Where a number is above / below / equal to some value, it switches to another style"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The leading is counted in “lines”. 1 is one line, 1.5 is one and a half. A line here is the line height the font decides, which is taller than the type's size (about 1.26 times). It is counted the same way as Word's and Writer's “multiple”, and differs from CSS's line-height."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Set a fill and please set the text colour too. Text with no setting takes “the screen's default colour”, so on a dark screen light text sits on a light fill and cannot be read."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Make” grows a new name. A name grown is listed under “Paragraph style” too."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Applying a theme"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The themes under “The whole document's theme” in the menu's “Style” swap "
    },
    {
     "text": "the colours and the fonts alone",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " as one set. Neither the spacing nor the sizes move."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The colours of the bars and the shapes switch apart from a table's rules and a heading's fill, because they are the colour of the contents themselves. Put the theme back to “Standard” and the colours are as they were at inserting."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Headings, the contents, and a chapter number"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A heading is not “a large, heavy paragraph”. What makes it a heading is giving the style "
    },
    {
     "text": "a depth",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Giving it a depth"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Open “The styles in detail” in the menu's “Style” and make the depth 1 for a chapter, 2 for a section. In this manual "
    },
    {
     "text": "chapter",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " is depth 1 and "
    },
    {
     "text": "section",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " is depth 2."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A chapter number is not written by hand"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Set “Bullets and numbering” to “A chapter number” and the number is "
    },
    {
     "text": "counted on every placing",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". A heading of depth 3 comes out as “1.2.3”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The numbers do not go into the document. So adding one chapter needs no retyping of the numbers behind it. This manual's chapter numbers are what was counted just now, too."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Putting the contents in"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "They go in from “Insert the contents” in the menu's “Insert”. What is inside does not go into the document; it is "
    },
    {
     "text": "assembled from the headings on every placing",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". Add a chapter and it grows by itself."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The drop is set by the indent of the contents' style. This manual's contents are at the very top."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The contents carry the chapter numbers, and a press on a row "
    },
    {
     "text": "moves to that chapter",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " (where it moved to comes out at the window's top). Point at it and the arrow changes. The same headings are listed in the navigation on the right, and a press there moves too."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "At the very top of the navigation on the right is "
    },
    {
     "text": "contents",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ". It is the way back from a chapter to the contents. After moving, the ribbon's "
    },
    {
     "text": "← Back",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " returns you where you were, and "
    },
    {
     "text": "→ Forward",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " goes on to before you went back."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Undo” takes a rewriting back; “Back” returns you to where you were looking. They are separate tools."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What the contents pick up is a style carrying a depth, and nothing else. They do not remember by name, so change a style's name and the contents follow along."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Bullet lists and numbers"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "To make a bullet list, open "
    },
    {
     "text": "Style",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " → "
    },
    {
     "text": "Paragraph style",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " and choose a style that carries a mark (in this manual "
    },
    {
     "text": "bullet",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " and "
    },
    {
     "text": "step",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ")."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The mark itself is not typed. The mark is carried by the style, so lay the style on and it comes out; change to a style with no mark and it goes."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There are four kinds of mark under “Bullets and numbering”. Every one is carried by the style, and none goes into the document."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The mark"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "What comes out"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "How it counts"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A mark"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The mark set (“• ” and the like)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It does not count"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A number"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "1. 2. 3."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It counts among the siblings that carry on"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A running number"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Figure 1. Figure 2."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It counts on through the whole document"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A chapter number"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "1.2.3"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It is decided by the heading's depth"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The numbers start the count at 1 again"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A number's mark counts “while the siblings that hand a number out carry on”. Let a paragraph that hands out no number in between and the next starts from 1 again."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "This comes out as number 1."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "This comes out as number 2."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Here an ordinary paragraph comes in between."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "So this starts from number 1 again."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A running number counts through the whole document"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A figure's or a table's caption is this. However much comes in between it counts straight on, so it runs on across the chapters as “Figure 1”, “Figure 2”. This manual's figure captions are those."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Taking a mark off is changing that paragraph's style to one with no mark. The mark cannot be taken off from the typing."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Tables"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A table is a block with “the style that lines things up in a grid” laid on it. "
    },
    {
     "text": "The document's side does not say “this is a table”.",
     "style": "strong"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Putting a table in, and moving from cell to cell"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It goes in behind the paragraph the cursor is in, from “Table” in the menu's “Insert”. Point at the grid there and the size lights up, columns first (“4 × 3” is four across); press the cell and a table of that size goes in, or press “Insert a table” for the size shown (2 × 2 to begin with). The grid reaches 10 × 8; a larger table is grown from the menu's “Table”, which is also what moves the cells themselves."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The command"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "What it does"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Insert a row / Delete the row"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Inserts one row below the cell you are in. What it deletes is the row you are in"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Insert a column / Delete the column"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Inserts one column to the right of the cell you are in. What it deletes is the column you are in"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Merge the selected cells"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Drag across the cells first, then press. Every one of them goes into the top left cell"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Unmerge cells"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Puts a merged cell back to the count it was"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Copy downward / Copy rightward"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Copies what is in the cell you are in to the one beside it. A formula's places shift with it"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Ascending / Descending"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "In the panel that “Order and narrow this column” opens, reorders the rows under the heading by the value in the column you are in, smallest or largest first. The first row is the heading and stays where it is"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Tab moves from cell to cell, and from the last cell it adds a row. Shift+Tab goes back one. Enter moves to the cell below and Shift+Enter to the one above, and from the last row Enter adds a row too. One undo takes a row added by mistake back. The arrow keys move too."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Scroll a long table and its first row stays at the top of the window until the table's last row comes up to it. Press it to go to the heading."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Showing only some of the rows"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Every heading cell carries a small arrow on its right. Press it and a panel opens under that column holding everything that orders and narrows it. The values the column shows are listed there with a tick beside each: untick the ones to leave out and press "
    },
    {
     "text": "“Narrow to the ticked”",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ". Only the rows whose cell in that column is one of the ticked stay in sight; the heading always stays, and so does the row you are in. A narrowing on another column narrows further. “Show every row” in the panel lets this column go, and “Show all rows of this table” under “Table” lets every column go at once."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The box above the list looks for a value; it narrows what the list shows and never changes what is ticked, so a search can be typed, cleared and typed again with the ticks untouched. The values come in the order that column sorts in, and the blank cells stand last as “(the blank cells)”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The same panel narrows by a condition instead: choose how the cell is to match (is, is not, contains, is above, is below, is empty, is not empty), type the value beside it, and press "
    },
    {
     "text": "“Narrow by this”",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ". One narrowing stands on a column at a time, so setting either takes the other off. A column that is narrowed keeps a line under its arrow."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The same panel opens from “Order and narrow this column” in the menu's “Table”, at the column the cursor stands in. There is one panel and two ways to reach it."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Narrowing is a way of looking, not a change to the document. It is not saved with the file, and a total still counts the rows you cannot see, as it does in Excel. The status bar says how many rows are shown while a condition holds."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Ascending and Descending at the top of that panel put the rows in order by that column. Sorting puts numbers first, then text by letter without regard to case, and empty cells last. A date in either spelling the formulas read sorts by the day it names. Where the sort cannot be done, the status bar says why: a cell merged down the page in the rows, fewer than two rows under the heading, or rows already in that order."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A merged cell decides no column's width. What does not fit inside it juts out."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Setting the width and the height"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A column's width and a row's height are "
    },
    {
     "text": "carried by the table",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " (not by the style). Drag a column's seam left or right, or a row's seam up or down, and they change. Point at one and the arrow's shape changes, so that is how a place you can take hold of is told."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "They can be set by number too. Lay the cursor inside the table and the fields "
    },
    {
     "text": "“A column's width” and “A row's height”",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " come out in the tools above. Type the same number and the columns' widths line up, so there is no matching them by eye. The unit is the same as the paper's and the margins': a point on the screen (px)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Empty the field and the setting comes off, and that column (or row) goes back to following its contents. The number showing faintly while it is empty is the width or height as it now stands, so you can tell what to start from."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press a seam twice and it fits itself to what is in it, the same gesture as Excel's. A column goes to the widest text in it; a row goes back to following its contents. A cell covering two columns is passed over when a column is measured, since its width is the pair's."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A width set does not widen for its contents. Text that does not fit juts out."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Merging cells"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Drag across the cells you want as one, then press "
    },
    {
     "text": "“Merge the selected cells”",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " under “Table”. Every cell the drag covered goes into the one at its top left, and the cursor stands there afterwards."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The text in the other cells comes off. Nothing is asked before it happens, because one undo (Ctrl+Z) puts every cell and its text back."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where it cannot be done the status bar says why: nothing selected inside a table, one cell alone selected, or a cell already merged that reaches outside what you selected. That last one is parted first with “Unmerge cells”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Taking CSV in and out"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Write the table out as CSV” in the menu's “File” puts the table you are in out. It goes in from “Insert from CSV” under “Table” in “Insert”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A table's formulas"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where a cell's text opens with "
    },
    {
     "text": "=",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " it is a formula. A place is written as the column's letter and the row's number, as "
    },
    {
     "text": "A1",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Trying a formula out"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press inside a cell and the field "
    },
    {
     "text": "Formula",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " comes out below the menu bar. Type "
    },
    {
     "text": "=A2*B2",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " into it and press Enter. Type the quantity in the table below over and the amount and the total both follow along."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The formula's field is shut while you are over the body. A formula can be written inside a cell and nowhere else."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "name": "detail",
   "columns": [
    64.0,
    64.0
   ],
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Qty"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Price"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Amount"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "3"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "120"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "=A2*B2",
         "style": "amount"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "5"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "80"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "=A3*B3",
         "style": "amount"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Total"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": ""
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "=C2:C3.sum()",
         "style": "amount"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Folding a range"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A range is written as "
    },
    {
     "text": "C2:C3",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ", with the way of folding it put on behind."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "sum() — adds them"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "count() — counts them"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "min() / max() — the smaller, the larger"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "avg() — the mean"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Pointing at another table by name"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Give a table a name and another table can point at it as "
    },
    {
     "text": "detail!C4",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ". The table below points at the one above."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The name goes on from "
    },
    {
     "text": "Set the name",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " under “Shape” in the menu's “Insert”, after clicking one of that table's cells. The name typed into the field goes onto that table."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What it goes onto changes with where the cursor is: inside a cell the table enclosing it, inside a slide's frame the frame, and otherwise the paragraph you are in. To put it on a table, please press inside one of that table's cells."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "name": "summary",
   "columns": [
    110.0,
    110.0
   ],
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Items"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Sum"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "=detail!C2:C3.count()"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "=detail!C4",
         "style": "amount"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A formula can be laid in the body too. The sum is "
    },
    {
     "text": "=detail!C4"
    },
    {
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Setting how a number is shown"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The digit grouping and the money sign in the “$1,000” on the amounts above are "
    },
    {
     "text": "set by the style",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". The digit grouping, the decimal places, per cent, the text put on before and after, and a date's shape can all be chosen."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The way of showing applies to a formula's answer alone. A number typed bare stays as it was typed."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Use “When the value” in “The styles in detail” and it switches to another style by whether a number is above or below some value (making it red, say)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Shapes, images and charts"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Putting a chart in"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Chart” in the menu's “Insert” makes bars or a line of a table's range. "
    },
    {
     "text": "What the document carries is the range alone; what is inside is assembled on every placing.",
     "style": "strong"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bar-chart",
   "chart": "detail!C2:C3"
  },
  {
   "style": "caption",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The detail's amounts made into bars"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Type the quantity in the table above over and these bars change with it. A chart remembers no values."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Drawing a shape"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It goes in from “Insert a shape” under “Shape” in the menu's “Insert”. The shape is carried by the style, and there are 11 (a rectangle, a rounded rectangle, an ellipse, a triangle, a diamond, and a line and an arrow each way up)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Set the name” puts a name on a shape."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Call it from the body” calls one from the body by number, as “Figure 1”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "On the ribbon, a button either does the thing at once or opens what has to be filled in first. “Table” and “Slide” go in on the press. “Image” opens the file chooser. “Link” and “Comment” open their field with the cursor in it, and Ctrl+K opens the link's field from anywhere."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Inserting an image"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There are two ways in. Both are inside the menu "
    },
    {
     "text": "Insert",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "For an image on your machine, press “Insert from a file” and choose the file. It goes in at the size of the image as it was read."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "step",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "For an image on the web, or one laid beside the document, type where it is into the field inside the same “Image” and press “Insert”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The size after it is in is changed by dragging the frame's corner. Write a number into the width and height fields before putting it in and it goes in at that size."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A file chosen, or an image dropped, is embedded into the document itself, with a local server running or not. An image typed by its place is pointed at, and only the place goes into the document."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "An image embedded makes the document heavy. The size embedded comes out on the status bar, so it can be noticed there. Embed many large images and it meets the ceiling for opening, and the document no longer opens."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "An image pointed at by place stops coming out unless the document and the image travel together. The HTML written out points at the same place, so move the page alone somewhere else and the image is gone. To hand over one file only, insert it from a file and it is embedded."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Slides"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A slide is a block with “the style that lays things at fixed places” laid on it. A frame inside it takes its place from "
    },
    {
     "text": "its own place",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ", not from the flow before and after."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Putting a slide in"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It goes in from “Slide” in the menu's “Insert”. The row of frames can be chosen from a layout (one frame, a title and a body, a title and two columns)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "slide",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "slide-title",
     "frame": {
      "x": 24.0,
      "y": 20.0,
      "w": 560.0,
      "h": 40.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "As one sheet"
      },
      {
       "text": " — showing the same tree, laid out differently"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "slide-body",
     "frame": {
      "x": 24.0,
      "y": 72.0,
      "w": 270.0,
      "h": 90.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "A frame's place is the coordinate from the slide's top left. It can be moved by dragging."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "slide-frame",
     "frame": {
      "x": 330.0,
      "y": 90.0,
      "w": 120.0,
      "h": 46.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "Prose"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "slide-frame",
     "frame": {
      "x": 480.0,
      "y": 90.0,
      "w": 120.0,
      "h": 46.0
     },
     "inlines": [
      {
       "text": "Slide"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "caption",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "One sheet laid in the flow"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Moving a frame, and taking one off"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press a frame and it is selected. Drag a handle and its size changes. What takes one off is “Delete the selected frame” under “Slide” in the menu's “Insert”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The frames of the slide you are in are listed in the navigation on the right. One can be selected and set there, and the order of overlapping sent forward or back."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Changing the slides' order"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "In the “Slides” tab of the navigation on the right, take hold of a thumbnail and carry it over another and it goes in there. Where it is going comes out as a dotted frame."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What carries the order is the document's row. So carrying one is the same as moving a paragraph inside the document, and one undo puts it back."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Putting them out in order (showing it in stages)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The frames can be put out one at a time in order. Into the "
    },
    {
     "text": "Step",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " field of the selected frame (in the ribbon's “The selected shape” group), write at which step it comes out."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "0 — it comes out at any time (this is the default)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "1 and above — it comes out when you have sent it on as far as that step."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "While it is being shown full screen, the key that sends on sends one step. Where no step is left it goes on to the next slide. There is one hand that sends."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What it carries is the order alone. It carries neither “it comes out after N seconds” nor an effect for the screen changing. Put time's axis into the document and something that copies to neither the paper nor the HTML written out is left inside it."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "So a page and the HTML written out are both always “the likeness with everything out”. Write a step and printing does not change."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Showing it full screen"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Slideshow” in the menu's “Share” puts them out one at a time, filling the screen. What sends on is "
    },
    {
     "text": "→",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " · "
    },
    {
     "text": "↓",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " · "
    },
    {
     "text": "Space",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ", what goes back is "
    },
    {
     "text": "←",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " · "
    },
    {
     "text": "↑",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": ". What stops is "
    },
    {
     "text": "Esc",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": "."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The style sets a sheet's size both ways. Write no width and it becomes the container's width, and how the frames sit changes with the window's width."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "subheading",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The presenter's notes"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press "
    },
    {
     "text": "N",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " while it is being shown and the note put beside that slide comes out at the screen's foot. Press again and it goes."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There is one screen, so the seats see the same thing. It carries no way of parting two screens and putting it out at your hand alone. So it comes out only while you hold the key down."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Notes, comments, links and attached notes"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There are four things that can be attached to the text you select. "
    },
    {
     "text": "None of them differs in how it looks; they differ in where they come out.",
     "style": "strong"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "What is attached"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Does it come out in the body"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Does it come out on paper and in the HTML"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A footnote"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A mark comes out, and it appears in the list too"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It comes out"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A comment"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It does not (it is remembered along with whose words they are)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It does not"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A link"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The text itself carries where it goes"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It comes out"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "An attached note"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A short note attached to a table, a slide or an image"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It does not"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Attaching a footnote"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Lay the cursor, put the text in under “Footnote” in the menu's “Insert” and press “Attach”. The number does not go into the document; it is "
    },
    {
     "text": "counted on every placing",
     "note": "So adding one footnote needs no retyping of the numbers behind it. This footnote is what was counted just now, too."
    },
    {
     "text": ". The list goes in from “Insert the footnote list” in “Insert”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "subheading",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Footnotes"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "footnotes"
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press a row of the list and it returns to where that footnote was attached. Point at it and the arrow changes. It is the same way as the contents."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Attaching a comment"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Select, then type it under “Comment” in the menu's “Review” and press “Attach”. It is remembered along with who wrote it (the name in “Comments by” beside it). "
    },
    {
     "text": "It does not come out in the flow",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " — it comes out neither in printing nor in the HTML written out. They are words somebody said about this text, and not the document's contents."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Attaching a link"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Select, then type where it goes under “Link” in the menu's “Insert” and press “Attach”. The blue and the underline are "
    },
    {
     "text": "carried by the style",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ", and where it goes is carried by the text. "
    },
    {
     "text": "Kanso's home page",
     "style": "link",
     "href": "https://kansosystem.org/"
    },
    {
     "text": " is one."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A link is not lost when its text is typed on. Unlike a formula, change the text and it still points at the same place."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Attaching a note to a table, a slide or an image"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press inside a table, a slide or an image, then type into the "
    },
    {
     "text": "Share",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " menu's "
    },
    {
     "text": "Attach a note",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " and press “Attach”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Each of them takes one note. It cannot be attached to a paragraph. It comes out neither in the flow, nor in printing, nor in the HTML written out."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A note attached to a slide is the presenter's note. Press N while it is being shown full screen and it comes out at the screen's foot."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Paper and printing"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It is set under “Paper and margins, the body's width, the header and footer” in the menu's “File”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The setting"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "What it does"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The paper's size"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A3, A4, A5, B5, Letter, Legal. Not splitting into pages can be chosen too"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The printing's bearing"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Upright or across. Chosen apart from the size"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The margins"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The room above, below, left and right"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The body's width"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It widens no further than this. At 0 nothing stops it"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The column's width and its left edge"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The width and place of the region the body is laid in"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The header and the footer"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The paper's header and footer. {page} becomes the page's number and {pages} the count of all the sheets"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where the paper's width is set, “the body's width” has no effect. The paper decides the width to print, so if both had an effect, two settings would decide a line's length."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "This manual begins as A4 upright with 15mm margins, and carries “{page} / {pages}” in the paper's footer. Set the page up front and the page breaks you see on the screen are the breaks that print."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It prints even left at “Do not split into pages”. Then it borrows A4 upright and splits it — unsplit, it becomes one long picture and the browser decides the page's breaks itself, partway down a line."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Making the body's width readable"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Make it a readable width” in the menu's “File” sets the width alone in one press."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Putting a header and a footer in"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Under “Paper and margins, the body's width, the header and footer” in the menu's “File”, text can go in that comes out at the paper's top and foot on every page."
    },
    {
     "text": "{page}",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " becomes the page's number and "
    },
    {
     "text": "{pages}",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " the count of all the sheets."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The alignment is set by the style. The names are “header” and “footer”, and the core sets those two, so another name affects neither. This manual aligns them both to the centre."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "With no room above and below there is nowhere to lay them, so the header and the footer do not come out on the paper."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Breaking the page"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Open “The styles in detail” in the menu's “Style” and stand "
    },
    {
     "text": "Break the page before this paragraph",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " up, and the page breaks before a paragraph of that style."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Turn it on in the chapter's style, and there is one place to change however many chapters there are. Turn it on in this manual's `chapter`, and every chapter starts on a new page."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "To break the page once only, "
    },
    {
     "text": "make a style named “page-break”",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " and lay it on that paragraph. It carries no separate machinery for breaking a page."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It has no effect in a document that is not split into pages, because there is no page to send it on to."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Printing"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It is “Print” in the menu's “File”. The grey dotted lines you see while editing, and the comments and the attached notes, do not come out."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The paper's size and bearing you chose come out in the printing as they are. Only the document's settings apply to the margins too (it does not lay the browser's margins over them)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Saving, writing out, and taking in"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There is one shape that can be read back, and several to write out. "
    },
    {
     "text": "What can be read back is “Save” alone.",
     "style": "strong"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Dropping it onto the screen to open it"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Drop a file onto the screen and it opens. "
    },
    {
     "text": "Drop an image and it is inserted at that place",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". What opens as a document is a file that is not an image. In Chrome and Edge, Ctrl+S writes straight back to the file dropped (Firefox and Safari open it, but saving drops a copy)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Beginning from a blank"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“New” in the menu's “File” opens a blank document in place of the one you have. No screen for choosing a template comes out. What you had not saved is kept as a draft, so nothing is lost (“The draft of what you were writing” below)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Neither the place to save nor the document's name is carried over, so that a blank is not written back to the file you had open."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The draft of what you were writing"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Shut it without pressing save and what you typed is still there",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". Where your hand stops typing, the text as it then stands is held back inside the browser. If a draft is there the next time you open it, the status bar tells you “There are N unsaved drafts”. It opens from “Bring the draft back” under “Draft kept” in the menu's “File”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A draft is not a save. Holding one back changes the file by not one byte. So it does not say “Saved” but only “Held back”. To leave it in the file, please press save as you always would."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A document brought back is tied to no file. A draft can be older than the file, so this is to keep one press from putting the file back to older content. Where it came from, the status bar tells you. The place to save is asked at the first save, and until then it stays a draft."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Once it saves to that file, the draft goes. The file carries it, so there is no need to hold it back any longer. Drafts you do not want can be thrown away together with “Throw the drafts away”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Open another document over one with changes not saved (by “Open”, “New”, the manual or a draft brought back) and "
    },
    {
     "text": "those changes are kept as a draft first",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". The status bar says so, and “Bring the draft back” brings them back at once."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A draft is inside this browser and nowhere else. It cannot be seen from another machine or another browser. Delete the browser's browsing data and the drafts go with it. A draft past 30 days, and the older ones beyond 32, are thrown away by themselves."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The command"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "What comes out"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Can it be read back"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Save (Ctrl+S)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The document and every style"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It can be read back"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Write out as HTML"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A block becomes an element, a style's name a class"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It cannot be read back"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Write out as Markdown"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The contents that hold text. Those that hold none become a comment"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It cannot be read back"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Open (a .md file)"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "A document made from its text"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Saving writes back to that .md"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Open a text"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": ".txt and a program's source"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Not one byte changes"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Write the table out as CSV"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The table you are in alone"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "It cannot be read back"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Opening Markdown has no “way of writing it cannot read”. A line it does not know goes in as a paragraph."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Open a .md file and saving writes back to that .md. It does not become JSON, so a document laid beside the code can be edited as it stands. Its diffs and its searches are the repository's own tools, unchanged."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What Markdown cannot carry (a page break, the columns, a comment, an attached note, a merged cell, where a slide's frames sit, a chart) is lost from the file written out. Where something is dropped, saving tells you how many."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A table's column alignment goes there and back. Left alignment written out plainly (:--) becomes the default (---), though; both look the same, so nothing has fallen away."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Open a file whose name is neither .kspage nor .md and it opens as a text (a .json saved earlier opens as a kspage document too). A .txt and a program's source are the same. Saving writes back to that file without changing one byte, so a compiler's or a tool's input can be edited as it stands."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A text stays as it was typed. The space at a line's end, the tab characters and a run of empty lines all stay, and a file that does not end in a newline comes back not ending in one. It neither adds nor evens up a newline at a line's end of its own accord."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Contents that are not text (an image, a program that runs) do not open. Opened, the screen would show garbled characters and the original file would break the moment it was saved. Where it refuses, it tells you in words apart from “too large”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A text carries line numbers. The number is the style's mark under “Bullets and numbering”, so take it off if you do not want it. The numbers are not written into the file."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A program's source carries no colours, in a file and in a Markdown fence alike. Its words, strings and comments come out in the one colour of the text."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Back” in the ribbon's “Move” group brings you back from where you moved to (a heading in the navigation, a row of the table of contents). Even having gone to another file, it opens that file afresh and returns to the line you were on before."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "One window holds one document. To see two documents at once, open the second in another window."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The colours do not go into the document. They come out in neither the file saved, the paper, nor the HTML written out, so they go once it is changed."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A text makes one paragraph of one line. It uses about 3 to 20 times the file in memory, so a very large file is refused before opening. Refused, the document you have is unhurt."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A document opened from a .md carries a way of showing from the start. A heading changes size by its step, a fence is fixed-width with a fill and a frame, a table is ruled, and a link carries a colour and an underline. The table of styles is the same as any document's, so change it after opening, or apply a theme, as you please."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The way of showing is not written into the .md. Change a style and the file's contents do not change, so save it and open it afresh and it comes out with the default way of showing again. To keep the look as well, please save as JSON."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Writing back to the same file"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It is “Save (Ctrl+S)” in the menu's “File”. To a file opened once by “Open”, or chosen at the first save, from then on it "
    },
    {
     "text": "writes straight back",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". A press never grows a copy."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It confirms the place to save only while it carries no file yet. From then on it does not ask."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Read the page afresh and the document you had open comes back, read again from its file, and it still writes back there. A tab opened anew starts from the sample, carrying no file."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "At the first save after reading afresh you may be asked to allow the writing. It is the browser itself that asks, so it cannot be avoided. Once the browser itself has been shut, even the reading wants the file chosen again with “Open”."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where the file it had open has gone, it says so and starts from the sample, carrying no file yet, so the next save confirms the place to save."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Only a browser that carries this can write back to a file. In one that does not, a copy is downloaded, and then it tells you so. It does not switch in silence."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Opening by a place in a local folder, and saving to that place"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "On a page opened from a server (kssrv) running locally, the field "
    },
    {
     "text": "“Path for saving and opening”",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " comes out on the second tier of the menu's “File”. Put the place as seen from the folder the server is serving in (a path such as docs/notes.kspage), press Enter, and it opens from there; “Save (Ctrl+S)” writes back there."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Read the page afresh and the document at that place opens again, so it does not confirm the place to save again."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Save with the field empty and it writes directly under the folder by the name on the menu bar, and puts that place into the field. The place to save is the folder chosen at start-up, so it does not ask."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where the same name is there already, it tells you rather than overwriting in silence. To overwrite, put it into this field."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "“Open” in the menu is the browser's own file window, with the server there or not. A document opened that way writes back to that file when you save, and this field clears, so what is shown is the one place it goes. A file chosen in the window may lie outside the folder being served, so it is reopened the way it was opened — by the window, or by a double-click."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where that file has changed outside after it was opened, saving refuses. Open the same file in two windows and save from both and one side's writing would go, so it does not overwrite in silence. Refused, please save under another name and open both to bring them together."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It cannot point outside the folder being served. Enter one and it tells you there and then."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The field does not come out on a page with no server standing. It puts out nothing that can be pressed and has no effect."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "kssrv puts one line out with the URL to open when it starts up. Please open it by that URL. The token is inside it, so type the address alone and the field does not come out."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Pointing at a document by URL, and opening it read-only"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Add "
    },
    {
     "text": "?doc=docs/design.kspage",
     "style": "code"
    },
    {
     "text": " behind the page's URL and it starts up with that document open. This is the shape that lets a README or a task sheet carry a link to a document."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Add "
    },
    {
     "text": "&read=1",
     "style": "code"
    },
    {
     "text": " as well and it opens "
    },
    {
     "text": "read-only",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": ". The tools that rewrite do not come out, and typing or deleting changes the document not at all. A link only meant to be read takes this shape."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What can be pointed at is a relative path as seen from the same place as this page, and nothing else. Another server's address (one opening with https://) and a path that climbs to a folder above are both refused."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The reading is an ordinary read, so it opens even from a server that only serves files. It need not be the local server (kssrv)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Read-only is not the document's property but a setting that depends on how it was opened. It comes out neither in the file saved nor in the HTML written out, so a document copied can be edited as usual."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Read-only can still find, move to a chapter from the contents, print and write out."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "On a page opened as a file (one opening with file://), ?doc= has no effect, because what it reads is not in the same place as that page."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Reading alone and editing can be crossed between at any time. Press the mode at the status bar's left edge and a choice opens with a mark on whichever it now is: "
    },
    {
     "text": "Edit",
     "style": "key"
    },
    {
     "text": " or “Read only”. A document opened with read=1 can be brought back to editing from there."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "warning",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "This is a screen against rewriting it by a mistaken press, and not a key. Please simply not hand over a document you do not want read."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Which it now is always reads at the status bar's left edge. Why a press has no effect is told there."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Naming the document"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Press the name on the menu bar and it can be rewritten. It becomes the name of the file saved."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Rewrite the name and it forgets where to write back. The next save confirms the place to save, and this is what “Save as” is."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Keyboard shortcuts"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "On a Mac, Command will do in place of Ctrl."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "table",
   "children": [
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "heading-cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "What it does"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Enter",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Parts a paragraph in two"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Backspace",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Deletes the one character in front. At a paragraph's head, joins it onto the paragraph in front"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Delete",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Deletes the one character after. At a paragraph's end, joins the next paragraph on"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "The arrow keys",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Move the cursor"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Shift+an arrow",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Select"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Alt+an arrow",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Move the selected frame or shape"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Home / End",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Move to a line's head or end"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Tab / Shift+Tab",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Move to the next cell or the one before"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Ctrl+A",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Select everything"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Ctrl+C / X / V",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Copy, cut, paste"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Ctrl+Z",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Undo"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Ctrl+Shift+Z / Ctrl+Y",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Redo"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "F4",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Do the last command again, where the cursor is"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Ctrl+B / Ctrl+I",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Bold, italic"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Ctrl+S",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Save"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Ctrl+F",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Find"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Esc",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "Clear the selection. Stop the slideshow"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "→ / ↓ / Space",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "To the next slide during a slideshow"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "style": "",
     "children": [
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "← / ↑",
         "style": "key"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "style": "cell",
       "inlines": [
        {
         "text": "To the slide before during a slideshow"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "chapter",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What it cannot do"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "body",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "kspage is not yet enough as an editing system. "
    },
    {
     "text": "What is missing is listed here.",
     "style": "strong"
    },
    {
     "text": " "
    },
    {
     "text": "It is so that you need not look for it thinking you have used it wrongly."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Reading aloud"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A screen reader cannot read the body. The body is drawn straight onto the screen, so to a screen reader it looks like one picture. The ribbon, the menus and the navigation on the right can be read, but the prose you wrote cannot be read from there."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A braille display cannot take the body either, for the same reason. It is not handed over as text, so changing the screen reader changes nothing."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "If you use a screen reader to read, please do not choose kspage. It is decided that the body is not handed over, and that will not change."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries no field for writing an image's alternative description either. The body does not reach the reading aloud, so what was written would have nowhere to reach."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Taking a document in from the three"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A Word file (.docx), an Excel file (.xlsx) and a PowerPoint file (.pptx) cannot be opened. There is no way of taking one in, so a document somebody sent you cannot be worked on here at all."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "None of the three can be written out either. What you wrote here cannot be handed to somebody who opens it in Word. What can be handed over is a printed page (PDF), HTML, Markdown, and a table as CSV."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A LibreOffice file (.odt, .ods, .odp) cannot be opened or written either."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where a table is what you want, CSV goes both ways (“Insert from CSV” under “Table”, and the writing out under “File”). The text goes across; the styles, the formulas and the merges do not."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where prose is what you want, Markdown goes both ways. What cannot be carried is written into the text as a note, so opening the result in any editor shows you what was dropped."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "How a document is made"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The depth carried into the contents cannot be narrowed. Every heading that carries a depth goes in, so the contents cannot be made of the chapters alone (that is why this manual's contents are long)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What a line's height was widened by all goes below. It is not parted above and below."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A number cannot be put inside a shape. A bullet or a number comes out at a paragraph's head, so it cannot be laid inside an ellipse or a rectangle."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The highlight fills the whole of the line's height, so widen the line and it does not fence the text."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A footnote comes out where the footnote list was laid, and not at the page's foot."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "At the first save after reading afresh, you are asked to allow the writing. Where to write back is remembered, but the browser itself asks every time, so it cannot be avoided."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There is a ceiling on the size of a document that can be opened. It is because the memory a page may use is fixed, and a document past it is refused rather than opened (and then the document you have stays as it is). The ceiling comes out in the debug log."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The ceiling is not decided by a count of bytes alone. It is decided by the “count” of a table's cells and of paragraphs too, so a document smaller than the ceiling can still be refused. A document parted finely into tables uses far more memory than prose of the same count of bytes (a table's cell is about five times a paragraph)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Where it refuses, the document you have stays as it is. What you were writing can never go. Please part the document and then open it."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What is wanting in the tables"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A formula can call eight workings by name (sum, min, max, count, round, year, month, day). There is nothing that looks a value up in another table by a key, and nothing that cuts or joins text. Where the work wants those, this is not the place for it."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Rows cannot be hidden by hand, nor gathered into groups that fold and unfold (Excel's Hide and Group). A filter narrows them by one condition per column, and it is a way of looking: it is not saved with the document, and a total still counts the rows it leaves out."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Only a table's first row stays in view as you scroll. A heading of two rows keeps its first alone, and no column stays put at the left (the page does not scroll sideways). On paper the heading is not repeated at the top of the next page, as Word and Excel can."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There is nothing that gathers a table into a summary by a key (a pivot table)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A range cannot be given a name. A formula points by the letters and numbers (A1, detail!C2), so what a range means has to be read from where it sits."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A table has no sheets. Where a workbook of several sheets is wanted, they become several tables in one document, each pointed at by the name it carries."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A chart is bars or a line. There is no circle, no scattering of points and no stacking."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A line break cannot be put inside a cell. A cell is one paragraph that wraps of its own accord; Enter moves to the cell below, as it does in Excel, and there is no key that breaks the line where you are (Excel's Alt+Enter, Word's Enter)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Sorting takes one column. Rows that tie on it keep the order they had; there is no second column to break the tie by, as Excel's “Then by” gives."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What is wanting in the slides"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries neither an effect for the screen changing nor an animation that moves an element. This is not something missing but something decided not to be carried (it copies to neither the paper nor the HTML written out). To put them out in order alone, the “Step” writes it."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A note for the speaker comes up while you are showing, with the N key, and it comes up on the screen the audience is watching. There is no second screen holding your notes and the timing while they see the slide alone."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There is no master slide. To make every slide carry the same title place and the same colours, lay the same style on each (change the style itself and every slide using it moves at once, so that is the way to do it)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Only one shape can be selected at a time. There is no selecting several to move or delete them together, and nothing that lines them up or spaces them evenly."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "No sound and no video can be put in. What goes in is a still image, the shapes and a chart."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "There are eleven shapes (a rectangle, a rounded rectangle, an ellipse, a triangle, a diamond, and lines and arrows). There is no line that joins two shapes and follows them, and nothing that builds a diagram out of a list for you."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What it does not answer about a program"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A program's source opens as plain text. Its words carry no colours, and nothing shows the place a symbol is in or draws what a file imports — please use an editor for those."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Nothing says a place that does not go through. There is no wavy line, no explanation floating over a name, no going to a declaration and no completion — please use an editor for those."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Renaming a name throughout cannot be done. “Replace” changes the text, so it changes the same letters inside a comment or a string too; please look at each one as you go."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Writing it with somebody else"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Two people cannot write into one document at once, on one machine or across a network. Whoever saves second is told the file changed underneath and refused, so nothing is lost in silence, but the two have to be brought together by hand."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Nothing keeps earlier versions or a record of who changed what. Keep a copy under another name, or keep the file where its history is kept (a repository such as git), and bring two together by opening each in its own window. Nothing sets two versions against each other or shows what changed between them."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Two documents cannot be shown side by side in one window. A window holds one document, so to see two at once please open two windows."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "Two places of one document cannot be seen at once in one window. Open the same file in a second window to read another place beside it."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "The draft of what you were writing"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A draft is not a save. Holding one back does not change the file, so to leave it in the file please press save."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What is held back is where your hand stopped typing. What was shut right after you began typing may not be held back yet."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "A draft is inside this browser and nowhere else. It cannot be seen from another machine or another browser, and deleting the browsing data deletes the drafts too."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It brings them back one at a time. They cannot be opened together."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "section",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "What it does not carry"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries no working for looking into a mistake in the text (a spell check)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries no way of setting the letter spacing and the line spacing finely."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries no vertical writing."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries no reading glosses."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries no mail merge."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries no way of writing a change as a suggestion for somebody else to take or refuse. A change goes into the document the moment it is made."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "bullet",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "It carries no documents to begin from (a template). A new document starts blank."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "style": "hint",
   "inlines": [
    {
     "text": "This list came out of writing this manual in kspage itself. It is what can only be known by using it, so please go on adding whatever you notice."
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "footer": {
  "style": "footer",
  "inlines": [
   {
    "text": "{page} / {pages}"
   }
  ]
 }
}